# HELP akash_canary_orphan_scan_degraded 1 when the fleet could not be fully enumerated, so the orphan count below is a FLOOR and not a measurement. The count is withheld entirely in that case -- a zero from a half-read fleet is a false all-clear.
# TYPE akash_canary_orphan_scan_degraded gauge
akash_canary_orphan_scan_degraded 0
# HELP akash_canary_orphans_total Deployments holding escrow that satisfy nothing. This is the paging signal. Reclamation is deliberately NOT automatic -- a wrong close destroys a live canary -- so this exists to put a human on it.
# TYPE akash_canary_orphans_total gauge
akash_canary_orphans_total 0
# HELP akash_canary_orphan_escrow_uact Escrow held by each orphaned deployment, in uact (micro-USD: 2000000 = $2.00). Labelled by dseq because that is the handle needed to close it and because a reaped orphan stops appearing, so no stale series is left behind at a nonzero value.
# TYPE akash_canary_orphan_escrow_uact gauge
# HELP akash_canary_orphan_escrow_uact_total Total escrow held by orphans, in uact. The per-dseq series above is for the human; this is for a spend threshold.
# TYPE akash_canary_orphan_escrow_uact_total gauge
akash_canary_orphan_escrow_uact_total 0
